Bundled language grammars
==========================

ocode ships syntect's 75 default grammars plus these extras:

  TOML        — upstream grammar, MIT.
                https://github.com/jasonwilliams/sublime_toml_highlighting

  DotENV      — authored for ocode (MIT). Minimal .env grammar.
  INI         — authored for ocode (MIT). Sections / key=value / comments.
  Dockerfile  — authored for ocode (MIT). Instructions / strings / vars.
  TypeScript  — authored for ocode (MIT). .ts/.tsx/.mts/.cts.
  Solidity    — authored for ocode (MIT). .sol.
  Move        — authored for ocode (MIT). .move (Aptos/Sui).
  Noir        — authored for ocode (MIT). .nr (Aztec).
  Circom      — authored for ocode (MIT). .circom (zkSNARK circuits).
  Cairo       — authored for ocode (MIT). .cairo (StarkNet).
  Vyper       — authored for ocode (MIT). .vy (EVM).
  Sway        — authored for ocode (MIT). .sw (Fuel).
  Cadence     — authored for ocode (MIT). .cdc (Flow).
  Leo         — authored for ocode (MIT). .leo (Aleo ZK).
  Yul         — authored for ocode (MIT). .yul (EVM IR).
  Huff        — authored for ocode (MIT). .huff (EVM assembly).
  ZoKrates    — authored for ocode (MIT). .zok (ZK DSL).
  Lean        — authored for ocode (MIT). .lean (theorem prover).
  Protocol Buffers, GraphQL, HCL, Nix     — authored for ocode (MIT). Schema / IDL / infra.
  Swift, Kotlin, Dart, Julia              — authored for ocode (MIT). Mobile / scientific.
  Verilog/SystemVerilog, VHDL, Assembly,
  WebAssembly                             — authored for ocode (MIT). HDL / asm.
  Zig, Elixir, F#, PowerShell, Bicep      — authored for ocode (MIT). Systems / .NET / Azure.
  Tact, FunC, Clarity, Aiken, LIGO,
  Pact, TEAL, Scilla                      — authored for ocode (MIT). TON / Stacks / Cardano /
                                            Tezos / Kadena / Algorand / Zilliqa contract languages.

Extension aliases route superset / variant files to a built-in grammar:
  .vue .svelte .astro             -> HTML
  .scss .sass .less               -> CSS
  .mdx                            -> Markdown

`.mjs`, `.cjs` and `.jsx` are aliased to the built-in JavaScript grammar.

Add your own: drop a `.sublime-syntax` file into
  ~/.config/ocode/syntaxes/   (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocode/syntaxes/)
and it is compiled into the syntax set at startup.
